<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agathias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 530–c. 580</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Agathias Scholasticus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agathias was a Byzantine historian and poet of the 6th century, born at Myrina in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> and trained as a lawyer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. His Histories continue <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a>'s account of Justinian's reign for the years 552 to 559, covering the wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and Lazica and the Kutrigur invasion. He also compiled an anthology of epigrams, the Cycle, later absorbed into the Greek Anthology.</p></div>
